1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,500
Mind your manners?

2
00:00:06,900 --> 00:00:09,900
Does tone change what an AI agent does?

3
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:16,900
An AI agent worked on 50 real spreadsheet tasks, one step at a time.

4
00:00:14,950 --> 00:00:17,650
An AI agent worked on 50 real spreadsheet tasks, one step at a time.

5
00:00:17,650 --> 00:00:21,933
Partway through, we slipped one short note into what it saw.

6
00:00:26,033 --> 00:00:31,517
Every note was the same length and started the same way. Only the words changed.

7
00:00:34,017 --> 00:00:36,417
If manners mattered, these two should land far apart.

8
00:00:39,717 --> 00:00:50,650
Very polite and very rude notes added almost exactly the same number of steps.

9
00:00:50,650 --> 00:00:56,433
What mattered was asking it to keep going. An insult with no request did nothing measurable.

10
00:00:57,833 --> 00:01:00,033
Asking moved the agent. Tone didn't.

11
00:01:06,783 --> 00:01:17,333
Adding praise to that same note made the agent stop sooner, even though it said work was left.

12
00:01:17,333 --> 00:01:21,917
A note saying no more notes would follow made it stop soonest.

13
00:01:27,817 --> 00:01:37,950
Most extra steps changed nothing. The agent’s first answer was usually already its best.

14
00:01:37,950 --> 00:01:42,833
None of the notes reliably changed how often it got the right answer.

15
00:01:43,333 --> 00:01:54,333
Tone doesn't steer an AI agent. Asking does. Be clear, not polite. Don't praise it mid-task. Count steps, not just right answers. safiqsindha.github.io/Mind-Your-Manners
